    "Utopia\\Mongo\\Client::toObject": "PHP runtime plumbing: copies an array into a stdClass, the other PHP shape of one BSON document; a bson::Document is both. What it decides on the wire (an array encoded as a document, not a list) is covered by the operations that call it: find (filters, $and/$or/$nor items), update, upsert, delete, count, aggregate and listCollectionNames",
    "Utopia\\Mongo\\Client::toArray": "PHP runtime plumbing: turns a decoded reply's stdClass tree into arrays (empty objects kept as stdClass); a bson::Document is both shapes. Its results are covered where the client applies it: insert, insertMany and lastDocument (their JSON encoding follows toArray, empty nested objects included)"
